M-Commander 6.1.0: avoid treating zsh RPROMPT as command input.

The embedded terminal reads input from the end of PROMPT to the right edge
of the screen. RPROMPT is included in that range even on an empty line, so
Enter runs an empty shell command instead of opening the selected directory.
Clear the right prompt in the embedded shell's precmd hook, after the user's
hooks. This is a compatibility workaround, not full right-prompt support.
No user startup files or outer-terminal settings are changed.

--- a/src/mcterm/mcterm_setup.c
+++ b/src/mcterm/mcterm_setup.c
@@ -92,6 +92,10 @@
         "}\n"
         "__mc_precmd(){\n"
         " local e=$?\n"
+        /* The host reads the command line from the screen after PROMPT. A right
+           prompt occupies that same range and would be mistaken for typed text.
+           Clear it after the user's precmd hooks, only in this embedded shell. */
+        " RPROMPT= RPS1=\n"
         " printf '\\033]133;D;%s;" MCTERM_MARK_TOKEN_KEY "%s\\007' \"$e\" \"$__mc_tok\"\n"
         " printf '\\033]7;file://%s" MCTERM_OSC7_TOKEN_PREFIX "%s\\007'"
         " \"$(__mc_pe \"$PWD\")\" \"$__mc_tok\"\n"
